            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0795" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13074: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-07T10:00:00+08:00">May 7, 1935—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 7—2:37 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>186. Reference Legation’s 184, May 5, 10 a.m.<anchor n="97" xml:id="d674-f1"/>
                    Following telegram has been received from the Vice Consul at Yunnanfu: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 6, 3 p.m. Reds crossing the Yangtze north of Mou, foreigners
                            returning Yunnanfu.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
